Package: lantern
Type: Package
Title: Ancestry-Specific Rare Variant Association Analysis
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Yu",
           family = "Wang",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "ywang@mcw.edu"),
    person(given = "Bjoernar",
           family = "Tuftin",
           role = "aut",
           email = "btuftin@email.unc.edu"),
    person(given = "Paul",
           family = "Auer",
           role = "aut",
           email = "pauer@mcw.edu"))
Description: Ancestry-specific rare variant burden testing for admixed
    populations. Splits genotype dosages by local ancestry (as inferred by
    'RFMix') into per-ancestry dosages, using either phased haplotypes or
    unphased genotypes with shrinkage toward global ancestry, and writes
    them to 'SeqArray' GDS files. Ancestry-stratified gene-level tests are
    then run with the 'SMMAT' framework of Chen et al. (2019)
    <doi:10.1016/j.ajhg.2018.12.012> as implemented in 'GMMAT', and the
    per-ancestry p-values are combined with the Cauchy combination test of
    Liu and Xie (2020) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2018.1554485>.
URL: https://yuw444.github.io/lantern/, https://github.com/yuw444/lantern
BugReports: https://github.com/yuw444/lantern/issues
SystemRequirements: bcftools (>= 1.10) (optional; faster VCF reading and
    BCF input)
